## Data layout (`/data/`)

The task bundle is mounted at `/data/`. Only the files listed below are
present — the original raw payloads from the upstream dataset are NOT
shipped (the install slicer materialises a single pre-split HDF5 bundle).

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `/data/dataset.h5` | Pre-sliced HDF5. Contains `train` (features + ground_truth), `test` (features only — `ground_truth` is held out), and root attributes `shape`, `split_policy`, `split_metadata_json`. Reference-shape unconditional generative tasks instead carry a single `reference` array. |
| `/data/load.py` | Trivial runtime loader; reads `dataset.h5` and reconstructs the dict the framework expects. The framework calls it for you via `task.load_data()`; you should not edit it. |
| `/data/task.py` | Defines `{{ class_name }}` (described in **Agent task interface** below). Import this class to interact with the task. |
| `/data/evaluator.py` | Assembled evaluator class `{{ class_name }}Evaluator`. The verifier runs it on submission; you do not call it directly. |
| `/data/task_rewards.py` | Reward classes the evaluator imports (curated bank subset plus any Phase-3-generated metrics for this task). |
| `/data/manifest.json` | Per-task descriptor: resolved reward names, expected output filenames, split policy, etc. |
| `/data/harbor_submit.py` | Submission helper (see **Submitting predictions**). |
{% if has_held_out_test_gt %}
The held-out test ground truth lives at `/eval-data/test_ground_truth.h5`.
That mount is **verifier-only** — your container has no read access to
it. The framework's `task.get_ground_truth()` method enforces this with
a `PermissionError` for auto-generated tasks.
{% else %}
This task uses a single shared reference distribution
(`split_policy="no_split"`); the agent and verifier read identical data
via the framework's reference accessors, and there is no held-out test
target. Distributional metrics like FID/KID compare your generated
samples against this reference.
{% endif %}
